# LIBM-ASINF-NODIV (D-10.103): asin on [-1/2, 1/2], the `float` asinf/acosf kernel without a
# division (Cody & Waite, Software Manual for the Elementary Functions, ch. 10): a polynomial in
# x for |x| <= 1/2, and the half-angle form asin x = pi/2 - 2 asin sqrt((1 - x)/2) above it, whose
# argument is again in [0, 1/2]. Odd powers up to 23; the x coefficient is fixed at 1 so that the
# leading term is exact.
name = fast32_asin
target = asin
interval = -1/2, 1/2
powers = odd 1..23
fixed = 1:1
error = relative
format = f64
output = crates/math/src/coeffs/fast32_asin.rs
